  "notes": [
    "Sony's PS5 launch release (2020-09-17, «DualSense™ Wireless Controller Specifications» table; read through sonyinteractive.com's own wp-json press-release API, which serves the page's content) prints «Approx. 160mm x 66mm x 106mm (excludes largest projection)» with «(width x height x depth)» on the next line; the en-gb store page agrees with labelled «Approx. H66 x W160 x D106 mm». Mass: the release's «Approx. 280g» and the CFI-ZCT1W instruction manual's «Mass Approx. 280 g» agree; the store page's «Approx. 0.3kg» is the same mass rounded to 0.1 kg, not a disagreement, so no conflict is filed. Controls (the release's «Buttons» rows, quoted in two parts because the table breaks the line; the middle rows read «Directional buttons (Up/Down/Left/Right), Action buttons (Triangle, Circle, Cross, Square), R1/L1 button, R2/L2 button (with Trigger Effect)»): dpad 1; face_button 4; bumper 2 (L1/R1); trigger 2 (L2/R2, adaptive); stick 2 (L3/R3 are clicks); button 4 = PS, Create, Options, MUTE; touchpad 1 (with its click). The CFI-ZCT1W manual's «Hardware part names» list (directional buttons, create, light bar, touch pad, player indicator, options, action buttons, two sticks, speaker, PS, headset jack, microphone, mute; top: R1, R2, USB port, L1, L2) matches. Ports: USB Type-C = usb_c 1; Stereo Headset Jack = headphone_3_5 1 (the store page says «the 3.5mm jack»); the «Charging Terminals» (contacts for the charging station) have no contract kind. wired=false: Bluetooth 5.1, USB for wired play and charging. The later CFI-ZCT2 revision has its own manual (mass also 280 g) but no Sony dimension line was found, so it is not filed. host_console uses the key sony-playstation-5-cfi-1000 (the launch model; any PS5 model hosts it)."
